<%# Sent after the fact: the rooms are already back on sale, so nothing here can
    be acted on to prevent it. It names the deadline rather than the agent --
    "we did not receive payment" reads as an accusation to an agent whose
    transfer is sitting unreviewed -- and gives both routes forward: rebook, or
    talk to the hotel. The eyebrow already says "cancelled", so the body does
    not repeat it.

    When money had already been paid, the mail says plainly what becomes of it:
    kept under the hotel's non-refundable deposit policy, or left for the hotel
    to settle with them. No refund is promised, because nothing is refunded
    without a person deciding it. %>
<% paid_note = if @payload[:paid_amount_label].blank?
                 nil
               elsif @payload[:deposit_retained]
                 "The #{@payload[:paid_amount_label]} you have already paid is retained by the hotel, as the deposit is non-refundable."
               else
                 "The hotel will be in touch about the #{@payload[:paid_amount_label]} you have already paid."
               end %>
<%= render "notification_mailer/agent_payment_notice",
      accent: "#b42318",
      eyebrow: "Booking cancelled",
      headline: "These rooms have been released",
      body: ["The payment deadline for this booking has passed, so the rooms have gone back on sale at #{@payload[:hotel_name]}. Search again in the portal to see whether they are still available. Already sent your transfer? Contact the hotel directly.", paid_note].compact.join(" ") %>
